{"data":{"issue":{"closedAt":"2026-08-26T18:26:37Z","state":"closed","notes":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"eyJjcmVhdGVkX2F0IjoiMjAyNi0wOC0yNiAxODoyNDoyOS45MjM2NzUwMDAgKzAwMDAiLCJpZCI6IjM3NDA5MjI1NTcifQ"},"nodes":[{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/1786152","username":"gitlab-bot"},"body":"@cleveland, our AI believes this is 72% likely to be a ~\"quick win\" (see [criteria for quick win issues](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/marketing/developer-relations/engineering/community-contributors-workflows/#criteria-for-quick-win-issues)), so we've applied the label. If this isn't a quick win, please remove the label.\n\n---\n\n[This message was generated automatically using AI](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-community/gitlab-org/quality/triage-ops/-/blob/master/policies/community/quick-win-judge.yml).","createdAt":"2026-08-21T22:13:34Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/316c04ca905dd31c1301cd74435c0b0cb6574693","resolvable":false,"resolved":false},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3718419876","lastEditedAt":"2026-08-21T22:13:34Z","lastEditedBy":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/work_items/8510#note_3718419876"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/1786152","username":"gitlab-bot"},"body":"We've attempted to automatically add labels to help route this issue to the right team.\nFurther tweak labels using our [community issue management UI](https://contributors.gitlab.com/manage-issue?projectId=34675721\u0026issueIid=8510\u0026action=label).\n\nHere's what our AI has to say:\n\n\u003e The existing category label 'Category:GitLab CLI' uses a different casing/format than the canonical 'category:gitlab cli' in the group::code review category set, but they refer to the same thing.\n\nWe believe everyone can contribute and welcome you to work on this proposed change, feature or bug fix.\nIf you are a new community contributor, start your [onboarding journey](https://contributors.gitlab.com) and get to know our community.\n\nTeam members, please indicate any mistakes by adding `/label ~\"automation:ml wrong\"`.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eView AI response JSON\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```json\n{\n  \"group\": {\n    \"existing\": \"group::code review\",\n    \"deduced\": \"group::code review\",\n    \"confidence\": 85\n  },\n  \"category\": {\n    \"existing\": \"Category:GitLab CLI\",\n    \"deduced\": \"category:gitlab cli\",\n    \"confidence\": 85\n  },\n  \"type\": {\n    \"existing\": null,\n    \"deduced\": \"type::bug\",\n    \"confidence\": 95\n  },\n  \"subtype\": {\n    \"existing\": null,\n    \"deduced\": \"bug::functional\",\n    \"confidence\": 90\n  },\n  \"areas\": {\n    \"existing\": [],\n    \"deduced\": [\n      \"backend\"\n    ],\n    \"confidence\": 85\n  },\n  \"note\": \"The existing category label 'Category:GitLab CLI' uses a different casing/format than the canonical 'category:gitlab cli' in the group::code review category set, but they refer to the same thing.\"\n}\n```\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n[This message was generated automatically using AI](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-community/gitlab-org/quality/triage-ops/-/blob/master/policies/stages/report/untriaged-issues.yml).","createdAt":"2026-08-21T22:13:54Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/18602a6353ea3e1bfa51e9875d95f9f390a1fa84","resolvable":false,"resolved":false},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3718420850","lastEditedAt":"2026-08-21T22:13:54Z","lastEditedBy":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/work_items/8510#note_3718420850"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/2935693","username":"phikai"},"body":"Investigated this. The bug reproduces, but the root cause is not in `glab` — it's in the Duo CLI binary, so this issue should move to [`gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab-lsp`](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab-lsp).\n\n## Why it isn't `internal/commands/skills/installed/installed.go`\n\nThat file can't produce the reported output:\n\n- `defaultCandidateLocations()` returns exactly two paths, `\u003cgit root\u003e/.agents/skills` and `~/.agents/skills`. There is no recursive workspace walk, so `agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.agents/skills/...` is never discovered as a second candidate.\n- There is no collision concept anywhere in `glab`. `Discover()` appends and sorts — no ✓/✗, no \"skipped\", no conflict type. `grep -ri collision --include=\"*.go\"` turns up nothing related.\n- `glab`'s scopes are `project` and `global`, not `workspace`. The reported output says `(workspace)`.\n\nConfirmed by building `glab` and running discovery against the symlink layout: one skill, one scope, no warning.\n\n`glab duo cli` only downloads and `exec`s a binary from project `46519181` (`gitlab-lsp`). The `workspace`/`global`/`plugin` sources and the `SkillConflict` type live there.\n\n## Actual root cause\n\n`packages/lib_ai_context/src/node/providers/agent_skills_resolver.ts` in `gitlab-lsp` already contains the fix this issue asks for — `#dedupeByCanonicalPath`, which resolves realpaths and drops duplicates (added 2026-07-29 in `fe4b628d`).\n\nThe problem is *where it is called*: inside `#findSkillsInRepo`, so it dedupes per repository. `#findSkillsInWorkspace` then does `repoResults.flat()` with no cross-repo dedupe, and `#findAllSkillFiles` concatenates.\n\nThat matters because `agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support` is a **git submodule** (mode `160000` in the duo-workspace tree), so two separate repos each independently find the same file:\n\n1. `StatelessRepositoryDiscoveryService.#findDotGitFiles` walks to depth 2 filtering on the *name* `.git`, which matches files as well as directories — so it finds the submodule's `.git` gitlink file. `checkIsRepo()` passes, so both the outer repo and the submodule are returned, sorted by path.\n2. The outer repo resolves top-level `.agents/skills` through the symlink → `.agents/skills/review-ticket-work/SKILL.md` (the ✓ winner, since the outer path sorts first).\n3. The submodule repo resolves its own `.agents/skills` → `agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.agents/skills/review-ticket-work/SKILL.md` (the ✗ loser).\n\nBoth are the same inode, but per-repo dedupe never compares them.\n\nVerified each link against a real submodule + symlink layout:\n\n```\ndepth-2 .git discovery:  ./.git  ./agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.git\nsubmodule .git is a FILE (gitlink), checkIsRepo → true\nSAME REAL PATH: True\nouter `git ls-files '**/.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md'` → empty  (git cannot see into the gitlink)\n```\n\nThat last line rules out the alternative explanation: the recursive `**/` glob is not what finds the duplicate.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nHoist the `#dedupeByCanonicalPath` call from `#findSkillsInRepo` up to `#findSkillsInWorkspace`, so it runs across every repo discovered in a workspace.\n\nKeep it workspace-scoped rather than moving it into `#findAllSkillFiles`: global and plugin entries carry `trustedRoots` for their containment check, and cross-source dedupe risks dropping the entry that holds that check.\n\n## Note on triage\n\nWorth moving rather than closing. As filed against this project, with a `~\"quick win\"` label and a confident root cause pointing at `installed.go`, a contributor is likely to spend time patching code that isn't involved.\n\n## Separate, unrelated observation\n\n`glab` does write *through* that symlink: in this layout `glab skills install` / `glab skills update` land in `agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.agents/skills/\u003cname\u003e/SKILL.md`, i.e. inside the submodule's working tree, showing up as an untracked change there. Possibly surprising, but not the bug reported here, and I did not investigate further.","createdAt":"2026-08-26T18:24:29Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/47f61eae8ef5b4973e8caadccfb2ea3320a26133","resolvable":false,"resolved":false},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3740922557","lastEditedAt":"2026-08-26T18:24:29Z","lastEditedBy":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/work_items/8510#note_3740922557"}]}}}}